    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_023f4745b60ec93875faf2b5dac6859becab92adbb87094c991b342bb3afbbd6",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The interacting dilation Hamiltonian reconciles bound-level and missing-line pictures by supporting both sectors at once: boundary transport closes allowed classical motion, its inverse leaves forbidden motion open, and the quantum Jost determinant distinguishes isolated normalizable states from the surrounding scattering continuum. The tuned two-boundary trap then demonstrates that the embedded levels arise by cancellation rather than from confinement by the free dilation operator.",
