    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_bb1e2c2b58bbe70ec7ae38755b3492db172dcae67dfd843a4b977f820499b6b2",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The paper refines spectral resolution while keeping the bulk dilation dynamics fixed: a Weyl area count supplies only the smooth density, Fourier-dual sharp boundaries turn the smooth functional-equation phase into asymptotic Jost resonances, and a Riemann-Siegel phase correction shifts the model toward individual zeros and changes the reconstructed localized waves. Each refinement adds boundary information rather than upgrading the original semiclassical count into an exact theorem.",
