      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_d3aabd6d7c9f4271a18491be1b1b5be32fbc69458470517488de3f86ad935c90",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Functional-equation duality organizes the model without closing its proof burdens: Fourier-related real boundary sectors generate the even/odd gamma phases, their Mellin amplitudes form a functional-equation-invariant sum, and Riemann-Siegel smoothing supplies a reflected pair of candidate boundary amplitudes. The remaining factor and analytic assumptions determine whether this phase construction is actually a Jost realization of zeta.",
